        "question_text": "<p>Rationalize the denominator of the expression <math>$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3} + 2}$</math> and simplify.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is <math>$\\sqrt{3} - 2$</math>.<br><math>$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3} + 2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 2}{\\sqrt{3} - 2} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{(\\sqrt{3})^2 - (2)^2} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{3 - 4} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{-1} = -5\\sqrt{3} + 10$</math>.</p>",
