        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>Given that <math>$x + 1$</math> is a factor of <math>$f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 + x - 6$</math>, find the other factors.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Since <math>$x + 1$</math> is a factor, use synthetic division to factorize:<br><math>$f(x) = (x + 1)(x^2 + 3x - 6)$</math>.<br>Factor the quadratic: <math>$x^2 + 3x - 6 = (x + 6)(x - 3)$</math> (incorrect; correct factorization is <math>$(x + 2)(x + 3)$</math> after re-evaluating).<br>Thus, the factors are <math>$(x + 1)(x + 2)(x + 3)$</math>.</p>",
