        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>Express <math>$\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}$</math> in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume <math>$\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$</math>.<br>Multiply through by the denominator: <math>$3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)$</math>.<br>Solve for <math>$A$</math> and <math>$B$</math> by substituting <math>$x = -1$</math> and <math>$x = -2$</math>: <math>$A = 2$</math>, <math>$B = 1$</math>.<br>Thus, the partial fractions are <math>$\\frac{2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$</math>.</p>",
