    "80889": {
        "order_id": 5,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Elective Mathematics",
        "topic": "Binomial Theorem",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the coefficient of <math>$x^3$</math> in the expansion of <math>$(2x - 3)^5$</math>.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the binomial expansion formula: <math>$(a + b)^n = \\sum_{k=0}^{n} \\binom{n}{k} a^{n-k} b^k$</math>.<br>Here, <math>$a = 2x$</math>, <math>$b = -3$</math>, and <math>$n = 5$</math>.<br>The general term is <math>$\\binom{5}{k} (2x)^{5-k} (-3)^k$</math>.<br>For <math>$x^3$</math>, set <math>$5 - k = 3$</math>, so <math>$k = 2$</math>.<br>The coefficient is <math>$\\binom{5}{2} (2)^{3} (-3)^2 = 10 \\times 8 \\times 9 = 720$</math>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
